  "body": "[\"serialize a JavaScript value to JSON bytes\"](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#serialize-a-javascript-value-to-json-bytes) implicitly treats a [\"string\"](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string) as a [\"scalar value string\"](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#scalar-value-string) (in fact, an [\"I/O queue\"](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-stream)), without mentioning how to handle unpaired surrogates.\r\n\r\nFortunately, ECMAScript guarantees that `JSON.stringify` will return a scalar value string, but that took a moment to verify. It would be nice to see this spelled out in Infra.",
